# The image installs the PUBLISHED package and copies exactly one file, so the
# build context should be close to empty. Without this, Docker uploads the whole
# checkout — node_modules, web/dist, the packaged app/ tree, the runtime — and
# the build spends minutes moving bytes it will never open.
#
# ⚠ Deny everything, then allow the one file back. An allow-list cannot be made
# stale by a directory somebody adds later; a deny-list silently can.
*
!docker/entrypoint.sh
